KG42.register("edges-44b99836e7090d0e80065176",{"id":"S-1b272357ba647227","source":"COMP-75186ff50e007d27","type":"links","target":"COMP-10be07664c6496b7","evidence_class":"S","scientific_acceptance":false,"relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"paper_ids":["22-decentralized_flexibility_markets"],"assertions":[{"id":"22-decentralized_flexibility_markets::v141-c-R003::E::v141-c-R003-E001","paper":"22-decentralized_flexibility_markets","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","rule_ref":"22-decentralized_flexibility_markets::v141-c-R003","record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R003-E001","source":"clearing.local","target":"coordination.price_signal","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R003-C001","v141-c-R003-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E10","v141-b-g02-e23"]},"evidence_class":"S","provenance_gate":"direct_C_edge_with_constraint_and_source_excerpt","scientific_acceptance":false,"accepted_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R003-C001","v141-c-R003-C002"],"held_constraint_ids":[],"semantic_review_status":"supported","source":"COMP-75186ff50e007d27","target":"COMP-10be07664c6496b7","source_occurrence_id":"22-decentralized_flexibility_markets::v141-c-R003::V::clearing.local","target_occurrence_id":"22-decentralized_flexibility_markets::v141-c-R003::V::coordination.price_signal","source_unit_id":"22-decentralized_flexibility_markets::v141-a-M01::clearing.local","target_unit_id":"22-decentralized_flexibility_markets::v141-a-M01::coordination.price_signal","omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"DSO buyer-side offers for unrealized flexibility contracts needed to meet distribution-network demand constraints. | Feedback from provisional local contract allocations during each iteration of distribution-network flexibility negotiation. | Initialization of buyer and seller prices for all potential flexibility trades. | Termination of the iterative flexibility price-negotiation process.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E10","v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e23","v141-b-g02-e24","v141-b-g02-e25"]},"active":true,"source_signature":"1f554ddf055f4708b2b12134984d672c6ee550c50fc18d0c39ed97a333d4b6c3","relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"source_science":{"mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","source_definition":"Iterative price negotiation coordinates agents' agreement on the local allocation of flexibility contracts. Scope: Completed day-ahead flexibility-contract allocation within one distribution network. Condition: Negotiation terminates when no price changes occur during an iteration. Deferred-acceptance agent-to-agent price negotiation can produce a stable local contract allocation when agent preferences are fully substitutable. Scope: Stable-outcome guarantee for the distribution-network flexibility market. Condition: Agent preferences satisfy full substitutability. Each agent selects a subset of its available contracts that maximizes its own utility. Scope: Individual contract-bundle selection by every agent in the local flexibility market. A feasible outcome associates each selected trade with at most one contract. Scope: Feasibility of the selected local flexibility-market outcome. The market should produce a stable allocation: no agent prefers to drop an associated contract, and no group prefers to mutually deviate to a different set of contracts. Scope: Desired outcome of the local flexibility market for the DSO, aggregators and prosumers. The local allocation should be Pareto efficient: no participant can be made better off without making another worse off. Scope: Efficiency requirement for local flexibility-market outcomes. Prosumer contract selection must respect resource power limits and energy-storage limits. Scope: Prosumer contract-bundle selection in the proposed flexible-resource model. At the end of price negotiation, the allocation satisfies the DSO's minimum and maximum total distribution-network demand constraints for each time interval. Scope: Distribution-network demand feasibility of the final local flexibility allocation. Condition: Prosumer resources have sufficient flexibility to satisfy the DSO's demand constraints. Each aggregator's total upstream and downstream contracts must balance separately in every time interval. Scope: Aggregator contract allocations in the baseline flexibility-market model. Condition: Aggregators do not consume, store or generate energy. In this extension, prosumer power and energy constraints replace the aggregator's per-interval upstream-downstream contract-balance constraint. Scope: Optional extension of aggregator contract-bundle feasibility to aggregators with their own flexible energy resources. Condition: Aggregator preferences are extended to represent their own flexible energy resources. Agents first select the minimum number of contracts needed to meet their constraints, then iteratively choose available adjustments providing the greatest utility increase. Selection terminates when none of the assessed adjustments provides further utility. Scope: Individual utility-maximizing contract-selection procedure within local clearing. Condition: Agent preferences satisfy the single improvement property.","target_definition":"The local contract-selection outputs identify an over-demanded trade for price-signal coordination, which increases that trade's seller price by Δp. Scope: Feedback from provisional local contract allocations during each iteration of distribution-network flexibility negotiation. Condition: The trade is selected by its buyer but not its seller, and its buyer price exceeds its seller price. The local contract-selection outputs identify an over-demanded trade for price-signal coordination, which increases that trade's buyer price by Δp. Scope: Feedback from provisional local contract allocations during each iteration of distribution-network flexibility negotiation. Condition: The trade is selected by its buyer but not its seller, and its buyer price does not exceed its seller price. Both buyer and seller prices for every trade are initialized to zero. Scope: Initialization of buyer and seller prices for all potential flexibility trades. Condition: Before iterative negotiation begins. Price negotiation is complete when an iteration produces no price changes. Scope: Termination of the iterative flexibility price-negotiation process. Condition: No price changes occur during an iteration. The DSO continues offering higher prices for unrealized contracts required to meet its demand constraints while those constraints remain unsatisfied. Scope: DSO buyer-side offers for unrealized flexibility contracts needed to meet distribution-network demand constraints. Condition: The DSO's demand constraints remain unsatisfied.","constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The local contract-selection outputs identify an over-demanded trade for price-signal coordination, which increases that trade's seller price by Δp. Scope: Feedback from provisional local contract allocations during each iteration of distribution-network flexibility negotiation. Condition: The trade is selected by its buyer but not its seller, and its buyer price exceeds its seller price.","expression":"Φ^{(k)} = {ω ∈ Ω | (ω, t_ω, p_ω) ∈ Y^{*,k}_{b(ω)} and ω ∉ Z^{*,k}_{s(ω)}}; ∀ω ∈ Φ^{(k)}, if p^{b,(k)}_{ω} > p^{s,(k)}_{ω} then p^{s,(k+1)}_{ω} = p^{s,(k)}_{ω} + Δp","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local","coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R003-X001","v141-c-R003-X002","v141-c-R003-X003","v141-c-R003-X004","v141-c-R003-X005","v141-c-R003-X006"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R003-T001","v141-c-R003-T002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E10","v141-b-g02-e23"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The local contract-selection outputs identify an over-demanded trade for price-signal coordination, which increases that trade's buyer price by Δp. Scope: Feedback from provisional local contract allocations during each iteration of distribution-network flexibility negotiation. Condition: The trade is selected by its buyer but not its seller, and its buyer price does not exceed its seller price.","expression":"Φ^{(k)} = {ω ∈ Ω | (ω, t_ω, p_ω) ∈ Y^{*,k}_{b(ω)} and ω ∉ Z^{*,k}_{s(ω)}}; ∀ω ∈ Φ^{(k)}, if p^{b,(k)}_{ω} ≤ p^{s,(k)}_{ω} then p^{b,(k+1)}_{ω} = p^{b,(k)}_{ω} + Δp","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local","coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R003-X001","v141-c-R003-X002","v141-c-R003-X003","v141-c-R003-X004","v141-c-R003-X005","v141-c-R003-X006"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R003-T001","v141-c-R003-T002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E10","v141-b-g02-e23"]}],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E10","location":{"location_id":"src-12c011a9b5-p03-c2r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II. Decentralized Flexibility Market Design","anchor_text":"eir their willingness to accept a contract specifying a price for a unit of of demand reduction duri","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"The agents reach mutual agreement on a set of agreed contracts and contract prices through an iterative price-negotiation mechanism. At each step of the market, agents select their favorite bundle of available upstream and downstream contracts, and over-demanded contracts have their prices increased. The process continues until no price changes occur during an iteration."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e23","location":{"location_id":"src-12c011a9b5-p06-c1r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"V.A Price-Negotiation Mechanism","anchor_text":"ω ∈Ω. The agents then engage in iterative negotiation with dow their neighbors. Each iteration: no r","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The prices of over-demanded trades are increased. The set of over-demanded trades is given by \\Phi = \\{\\omega \\in \\Omega \\mid (\\omega, t_{\\omega}, p_{\\omega}) \\in Y^{*}_{b(\\omega)}, \\omega \\notin Z^{*}_{s(\\omega)}\\}. For each \\omega \\in \\Phi, if p^{b}_{\\omega} > p^{s}_{\\omega}, then p^{s}_{\\omega} is increased by \\Delta p; otherwise, p^{b}_{\\omega} is increased by \\Delta p."}],"omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"DSO buyer-side offers for unrealized flexibility contracts needed to meet distribution-network demand constraints. | Feedback from provisional local contract allocations during each iteration of distribution-network flexibility negotiation. | Initialization of buyer and seller prices for all potential flexibility trades. | Termination of the iterative flexibility price-negotiation process.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E10","v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e23","v141-b-g02-e24","v141-b-g02-e25"]},"source_record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R003-E001","source":"clearing.local","target":"coordination.price_signal","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R003-C001","v141-c-R003-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E10","v141-b-g02-e23"]},"paper_scope_note":"The temporarily selected excess-demand feedback differs from the final contract configuration; the final price-to-payment relation is limited to the same concluded contract and metering interval."}}],"assertion_ids":["22-decentralized_flexibility_markets::v141-c-R003::E::v141-c-R003-E001"]});
